// Title: Removal Of SD Value to Hide Schedule Task - Registry
// Sigma ID: acd74772-5f88-45c7-956b-6a7b36c294d2
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Sittikorn S
// Date: 2022-04-15 | Modified: 2025-10-25
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Remove SD (Security Descriptor) value in \Schedule\TaskCache\Tree registry hive to hide schedule
//   task. This technique is used by Tarrask malware
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2022/04/12/tarrask-malware-uses-scheduled-tasks-for-defense-evasion/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_delete/registry_delete_schtasks_hide_task_via_sd_value_removal.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (ActionType in~ ("RegistryKeyDeleted", "RegistryValueDeleted")) and (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Schedule\\TaskCache\\Tree.*$" and RegistryKey contains "SD")
